# Auth & guest

## Session restore

`Routes.jsx` loads `STORAGE_KEYS.USER_DATA`. Presence of `accessToken` selects Main vs Auth.

## Gate actions / screens

```js
// Action-level
const { requireAuth, isGuest } = useAuth();
if (!requireAuth("Sign in to continue")) return;

// Screen-level
useGuestScreenGuard();
```

Or `requireAuth(dispatch, isGuest, message)` from `utils/authHelpers.js`.

## Guest restrictions

Guests have a token but cannot open routes in `GUEST_RESTRICTED_SCREENS`. `Routes` also bounces guests via `onStateChange` → `exitGuestForSignIn`.

**When adding a gated screen:** add its `navigationStrings` name to that Set.

## Session expiry

Handled in `apiClient` → `handleSessionExpired` / `expireSession`. Do not invent a parallel logout path for 401s.

## Storage keys

Use `STORAGE_KEYS` from `utils/storageKeys.js` (`USER_DATA`, `TOKEN`, onboarding flags, etc.).
